  "sourceIndex": {
    "candidate": "No complete retained target context found in designated predecessor indexes. Historical Britannica HTTP 206 metadata has no retained body and is not proof; URL not reopened.",
    "options": "Each option/note was checked against a full captured institutional page; exact locators bind all six literal groups.",
    "coverage": "All six groups and four full triples map to complete visible page outputs. The archive and Presidential Library identify the Novgorod Chronicle as the primary account; official history entry names Teutonic Order knights."
  },
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "history-russia-alexander-nevsky-battle",
      "status": "READY_FOR_SAME_READER_FINAL",
      "beforeHash": "59439044965ca499a42041e4dc0426e84a1de0a656f3951055c09882ee118717",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "С каким противником сражался Александр Невский в Ледовом побоище?",
            "answers": [
              "Османскими янычарами",
              "Рыцарями Тевтонского ордена",
              "Шведскими викингами",
              "Французской армией"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 1
          },
          "literalSHA256": "04fd119d832255561c772b4a4042fb2ac93beca0958840676bece65d4d870658",
          "primaryGround": "Presidential Library identifies Teutonic Order knights at the 1242 Lake Peipus battle (L42-L44); it identifies the Novgorod Chronicle as a primary account (news L45-L48). The distractors belong to distinct contexts: Janissaries are Ottoman elite infantry, the Swedish History Museum dates its Viking exhibit to 750–1100, and Grand Palais dates Napoleon’s Russian campaign to 1812. Only the Teutonic knights fit the prompt.",
          "locator": "turn3view0 L42-L46; turn3view1 L45-L48; turn3view3 L65-L74; turn5view1 L79-L82; turn3view4 L38-L41",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/academia-and-vikings-open.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "В Ледовом побоище 1242 года войско Александра Невского сражалось с рыцарями Тевтонского ордена. Битва произошла на Чудском озере.",
          "literalSHA256": "6c0741dfbee35d517c815fd5ee5809d6458a5a4813f2c829b2bddd41c40d5fa2",
          "primaryGround": "The Presidential Library identifies the 1242 Lake Peipus battle and Teutonic Order knights; the Institute archive independently confirms Lake Peipus and identifies its preserved Commission copy of the Novgorod First Chronicle.",
          "locator": "turn3view0 L42-L44; turn5view0 L13",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/academia-and-vikings-open.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Янычары были элитной пехотой Османской империи.",
          "literalSHA256": "966ca253d336288c5442d526ca4be482f7dffe323b1080c69b1dc81708a2d282",
          "primaryGround": "Museum object page identifies the period/dynasty as Ottoman and describes Janissaries as Turkish elite infantry.",
          "locator": "turn3view3 L65-L74",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note1",
          "literal": "В летописном описании построение орденского войска названо «свиньёй», то есть клином.",
          "literalSHA256": "118c0265b77079e3d85d2465db91b357cf28878bfcb3fe947e75209e01fd2d8a",
          "primaryGround": "The Presidential Library’s summary of the Novgorod Chronicle names the order-army formation “pig” and glosses it as a wedge; this detail is absent from prompt and explanation.",
          "locator": "turn3view1 L45-L48",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15d80/source-history-russia15/raw/prlib-battle-mixed-open.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
